    {
      "id": "claim_33b705f9e4b344a684c222f28044661a",
      "statement": "After the engine returns a SearchIndexBatchResult, partitionOutcomes maps each mutation's outcome to its outbox rows: applied mutations are acked (processed_at set), failed mutations are blamed (retry_count+1, last_error, dead-lettered at maxAttempts), and unapplied mutations are released unblamed; all post-claim updates are fenced by claim_token.",
