      "statement": "Projection state (hash + applied_sequence) is persisted after the index write and before the ack; a crash in between re-claims the rows and re-derives 'unchanged' from the persisted hash. State writes are generation-scoped: an old generation can never overwrite a newer generation's state (compare-and-set on generation + applied_sequence).",
